# Exercise: Parallel Speedup
#
# Amdahl's Law: Speedup = 1 / ((1-p) + p/n)
#
# Now let's parallelize! With 2 workers processing 4 items
# (10ms each), the parallel portion finishes faster.
#
# Serial time: 4 x 10ms = 40ms
# Parallel (2 workers): 2 batches x 10ms = ~20ms for parallel work
#
# But there's always some serial overhead (sending items,
# collecting results). So actual speedup < 2x.
#
# Your task: Process 4 items with 2 workers, verify all complete.
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: test-parallel-speedup ( -- )
    chan.make   # work
    chan.make   # results

    # Spawn 2 workers: each processes 2 items
    2dup [ over chan.receive drop 10 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ over chan.send drop
           over chan.receive drop 10 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ over chan.send drop
           drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
    drop drop
    2dup [ over chan.receive drop 10 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ over chan.send drop
           over chan.receive drop 10 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ over chan.send drop
           drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
    drop drop

    # Send 4 items
    over 10 swap chan.send drop
    over 20 swap chan.send drop
    over 30 swap chan.send drop
    over 40 swap chan.send drop

    # Your code here:
    # Receive 4 results and sum them
    # Expected: 11 + 21 + 31 + 41 = 104
    drop drop 0

    # Do not edit below this line
    104 test.assert-eq
;
